const r={observe:{tone:"info"},advise:{tone:"info"},enforce:{tone:"warn"},off:{tone:"neutral"},disabled:{tone:"neutral"}},a={blocked:{tone:"danger"},confirmed:{tone:"info"},warned:{tone:"warn"},redacted:{tone:"accent"},allowed:{tone:"neutral"},degraded:{tone:"warn"},detected:{tone:"danger"}};function s(e){return e.startsWith("degraded:")?"degraded":e}const i={applied:{tone:"success"},fail_closed:{tone:"danger"},breaker_open:{tone:"danger"},upstream_error:{tone:"danger"},fallback_open:{tone:"warn"},splice_failed:{tone:"warn"}},d={ok:{tone:"success"},warn:{tone:"warn"},fail:{tone:"danger"}},t={ok:{tone:"success",tip:"Commit capture is live for this project.",banner:"",todo:"",rescan:!0},catching_up:{tone:"info",label:"catching up",tip:"Reading this project's full git history in the background. Recent commits are already in.",banner:"Reading this project's full git history",todo:"A large history is read in steps of about 45 seconds per scan. Recent commits are in already, so the figures below use them. Nothing to do.",rescan:!0},never_scanned:{tone:"warn",label:"not scanned",tip:"The commit scanner hasn't scanned this project yet.",banner:"Not scanned yet",todo:"The scanner reads every project with a session in the last few days, every 2 minutes. Rescan now to read it immediately.",rescan:!0},no_git:{tone:"warn",label:"no git",tip:"git is not installed (or not on PATH) for the Observer daemon.",banner:"git is not installed",todo:"Install git and make sure it is on the PATH of the user that runs Observer, then restart the daemon.",rescan:!1},no_folder:{tone:"warn",label:"no folder",tip:"This project has no folder on disk: the tool did not report one, so there is no repository to read.",banner:"This project has no folder on disk",todo:"The AI tool filed these sessions under a placeholder name instead of a folder. Nothing to fix here: commits for this work show on the project for its real folder.",rescan:!1},root_missing:{tone:"warn",label:"folder gone",tip:"The project folder was deleted, moved or is not mounted. Commits captured before are kept.",banner:"The project folder was not found",todo:"It was deleted, moved, or is on a drive that is not mounted right now. Commits captured before are kept. If you moved it, the next session in the new place starts a new project; if it comes back, scanning resumes on its own.",rescan:!0},not_repo:{tone:"warn",label:"not a repo",tip:"The folder exists but is not a git repository.",banner:"This folder is not a git repository",todo:"Commit tracking needs git. Run git init (or clone the project) in this folder; the scanner re-checks every 30 minutes, or rescan now.",rescan:!0},error:{tone:"warn",label:"scan error",tip:"The last commit scan failed. Open the project for the reason.",banner:"The last commit scan failed",todo:"",rescan:!0}},o={timeout:{what:"git took too long, even when asked for a few commits at a time",todo:"Usually a very large repository on a slow drive (for example /mnt/c from WSL). Rescan now to try again; moving the repository to the Linux file system makes it much faster."},dubious_ownership:{what:"git refused the folder because another user owns it",todo:"Common for /mnt/c folders seen from WSL. If you trust the folder, run: git config --global --add safe.directory <folder>, then rescan."},permission_denied:{what:"the folder or its .git directory is not readable by the user Observer runs as",todo:"Fix the folder permissions, then rescan."},repo_unreadable:{what:"git reports a missing or damaged object in this repository",todo:"Run git fsck in the folder. A shallow or partial clone can also cause this; fetching the full history fixes it."},output_too_large:{what:"a single commit's change summary is larger than the scanner's 8 MB limit",todo:"This is rare (usually a huge generated file committed once). Recent commits around it are still captured."},other:{what:"git failed for a reason the scanner does not recognise",todo:"The message from git is below. Rescan to retry; it also retries on its own with a growing delay."}},c={info:{tone:"info"},advice:{tone:"accent"},warning:{tone:"warn"}},l={cost:{tone:"neutral"},latency:{tone:"neutral"},quality:{tone:"neutral"},hygiene:{tone:"neutral"}},h={session:{tone:"neutral"},project:{tone:"neutral"},global:{tone:"neutral"}},f={intact:{tone:"success",label:"ok"},broken:{tone:"danger"}};function m(e){return e.commits==="error"?`The last commit scan failed: ${(o[e.commits_kind??"other"]??o.other).what}. Open the project to see what to do.`:(t[e.commits]??t.error).tip}export{f as A,d as C,i as E,r as P,l as S,t as a,o as b,a as c,h as d,c as e,m as f,s as p};
